On Thursday 18 August 2011 22:59:08 Jed wrote:
> Why is "lo ponskina" okay? Just because it ends in a full-length
> gismu?

"ponskina" is a selbri. It is a brivla, more precisely a lujvo, but there are 
other kinds of selbri, and they too can be preceded by "lo": lo kernauke, lo 
pamoi, lo me la ponkin, lo jukni julne, lo nu mi pilno lo skami, etc.

